& [Purpose] is reliable tool-contract transport
  + publish exact machine-readable syntax for prepare, run, verify, and their responses
  + let CLI, future MCP, and provider-tool projections share one form and one canonical schema source
  + make schema drift, projection loss, and semantic residuals inspectable

& [ThreeGateModel] is constitutional
  + gate_1 syntactic conformance is JSON Schema plus strict serde agreement
  + gate_2 semantic conformance is existing Cantor validation, digest recomputation, referential integrity, bounds, causal replay, and policy checking
  + gate_3 authority admission is recognized principal, generation, scope, and effect authorization
  + passing gate_1 does not imply gate_2 or gate_3
  + passing gate_2 does not imply gate_3

& [SharedTransportForms] remove private duplication
  + move prepare, run, verify, response, fault, verification, status, profile, and exit projections into one transport-neutral library surface
  + the library performs no filesystem, stdin, stdout, provider, service, or network operation
  + existing CLI imports the shared forms and pure dispatch semantics
  + extraction must preserve all pushed schema, prepare, run, verify, fault, JSON, and exit behavior exactly

& [CanonicalDialect] is provider neutral
  + JSON Schema dialect is https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema
  + canonical schema uses no provider-private extension
  + every object is closed with additionalProperties false unless its type is an explicit map
  + property requirement, omission, and nullability match actual serde behavior
  + enum representation, tags, and values match actual serde behavior
  + numeric and collection bounds are represented when structurally knowable

& [Canonicalization] is deterministic
  + recursively sort object keys by Unicode scalar value sequence
  + retain array order because it is semantic
  + encode compact UTF-8 JSON without insignificant whitespace
  + reject duplicate JSON object keys before normalization
  + compute SHA-256 over exact canonical bytes
  + equal shared forms, generator version, options, and source revision produce byte-identical schemas and bundle

& [SchemaDocuments] are content bound
  + stable schema id uses urn:cantor:schema:<profile>:<type-name>
  + each document identifies type, dialect, profile, generator, source revision, canonical byte length, and SHA-256
  + shared definitions use stable type names rather than compiler path spelling
  + recursive and mutually referenced definitions are rejected in profile 0.1 unless a finite resolved representation is separately proven

& [Bundle] is one compatibility unit
  + contains prepare input, run input, verify input, base response, preparation response, and shared definitions
  + contains per-type fingerprints and exact semantic residual references
  + contains generator identity and source commit
  + contains compatibility baseline and bundle digest
  + unknown or missing required member invalidates the bundle

& [SemanticResidualRegistry] is mandatory
  + identify cross-field and graph rules not proven by syntax
  + name the exact core enforcement stage and function when implemented
  + distinguish invalid syntax, semantically invalid value, refused authority, and unimplemented enforcement
  + a provider projection repeats all residuals or explicitly declares that the controller must retain them

& [Conformance] uses two independent readers
  + validate each case through the canonical JSON Schema engine
  + decode the same case through the actual strict serde form
  + require agreement for every syntax rule claimed expressible
  + separately run semantic validation where a complete safe fixture exists
  + positive, minimum, maximum, missing, null, unknown, duplicate-key, wrong-type, wrong-tag, wrong-enum, and excessive-cardinality cases are required
  + disagreement is a release-blocking typed fault, not an undocumented exception

& [Compatibility] is explicit
  + compare canonical schema paths and accepted-value implications between exact old and new bundle digests
  + classify each operation input and output as identical, proven compatible in the declared direction, or breaking
  + residual additions, removals, or enforcement-stage changes are reported separately
  + unknown compatibility is breaking for activation purposes

& [ProviderNeutralToolDefinitions] are structural only
  + define distinct names for prepare, run, and verify
  + each definition references exact canonical input and output schema digests
  + annotations declare read-only host behavior, deterministic replay, experiment grade, and no open-world effect
  + descriptions preserve stop-call-result-later-pass semantics and residuals
  + tool definitions do not execute a model, open MCP, or contact a provider

& [ProviderProjection] is later and lossy-aware
  + each provider profile declares supported dialect subset, rewrites, omitted constraints, external validators, size limits, and exact canonical source digest
  + projection cannot weaken core semantic or authority gates
  + provider acceptance is not canonical acceptance until the returned arguments pass strict serde and Cantor validation

& [Bounds] are finite
  + schema bundle byte size, definition count, reference count, nesting depth, property count, enum count, residual count, and conformance corpus size have explicit limits before implementation
  + generator fails closed on limit exhaustion
  + no network reference resolution is allowed

& [ImplementationSequence] is dependency ordered
  + CPMS-I01 public transport-neutral forms and exact CLI byte equivalence
  + CPMS-I02 canonical Draft 2020-12 generation, normalization, digest, and limits
  + CPMS-I03 semantic residual registry and schema-serde conformance corpus
  + CPMS-I04 provider-neutral prepare run verify tool-definition bundle with no provider
  + CPMS-I05 compatibility and release audit
  + no later slice is ready before the preceding reviewed proof closes

& [Proof] is multi-layered
  + compile-time shared type use prevents CLI and schema wrappers from diverging silently
  + golden canonical schemas are content addressed
  + independent parser rejects duplicate keys and validates canonical documents
  + conformance corpus demonstrates schema-serde agreement within claimed coverage
  + source scan and runtime counters prove zero provider, model, network, persistence, service, effect, and hardware behavior
  + full workspace debug, overflow-checked release, offline, lint, documentation, and advisory gates pass

& [HonestyLimits] are explicit
  + exhaustive schema-serde equivalence over infinite values is not claimed
  + JSON Schema does not prove digest correspondence, reference existence, causal integrity, truth, safety, permission, or production fitness
  + derive-macro output is evidence only after canonicalization and conformance tests
  + tool descriptions are guidance and not authority

& [FormationBoundary] is no implementation authority
  + this canonical is formed for review and future slice signatures
  + implementation requires exact canonical hash binding and a separately claimed CPMS slice
  - never: infer live MCP, provider registration, model execution, llama.cpp modification, hidden-state sharing, service, persistence, network, external semantic effect, hardware, FPGA, or production release

